invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: after a switch the Initial level admits the negotiated version
  alone, so a client drops the server's Initial packets in the original
  version, which a server sends until it has processed the client's
  transport parameters (rfc9369.txt:246-248). test/quic_version_tests.h
  switches a version 1 client to version 2 and requires a server Initial
  packet in version 1 to open.

--- old
    return level == CH_LEVEL_INITIAL && version == q->t.cfg.quic_original_version;
--- new
    return level == CH_LEVEL_INITIAL && version == q->t.quic_negotiated_version;
